# SPA fallback. One line per top-level route in src/app/routes.ts.
#
# ⛔ THE DESTINATION MUST BE `/`, NEVER `/index.html`. Cloudflare Pages strips
# `.html` and `index` from URLs, so any rule pointing at /index.html is either
# rejected outright ("Infinite loop detected in this rule and has been ignored")
# or, for a non-wildcard source, silently downgraded from a 200 rewrite to a
# 308 REDIRECT to `/` — which drops the path and lands every shared deep link on
# the homepage. Measured in `wrangler pages dev`, which reproduces production.
#
# ⛔ AND THERE IS NO CATCH-ALL. `/*` matches `/` itself, which is what trips the
# loop detector; the previous single line `/*  /index.html  200` parsed as ZERO
# valid rules, so nothing here was in effect at all. Routes are listed
# explicitly instead — tests/test_capture_demo_dataset.py::
# test_every_route_has_a_spa_redirect_rule fails when routes.ts gains one that
# is missing here.
#
# Unlisted paths still 404 to public/404.html, which parks the URL and bounces —
# correct for genuine typos, and the only mechanism GitHub Pages has.
# ⚠️ Do not delete 404.html to "let Pages do SPA routing": tested, and Pages then
# serves a bare contentless 404 for every deep link.

/browse/*       /   200
/prices/*       /   200
/product/*      /   200
/category/*     /   200
/browse         /   200
/search         /   200
/deals          /   200
/favorites      /   200
/alerts         /   200
/account        /   200
/auth           /   200
/privacy        /   200
/terms          /   200
/cookie-policy  /   200
/contact        /   200
/compare        /   200
/style-guide    /   200
